  "body": "The first full visual evaluation of the original 947,712-parameter action adapter after sixteen paired training updates failed to follow commands. Both 1248 \u00d7 704 clips preserve a recognizable room but keep the door closed and framing nearly static, despite different first interaction commands and the requested subsequent left turns. All 34 frames were inspected. Both generated clips have higher average future RGB error against the intended capture than repeating the starting image. This is a failed action-control result, not Genie 3 parity or a scientific breakthrough.\n\nThe complete paired run took 420.010 seconds, including original foundation loading, before/after checks and decoding. Sampling each 17-frame clip took about 44 seconds, with exactly 50 native UniPC steps, shift 5 and guidance 5. GIF playback at 120 ms per frame is unrelated to generation speed. The two arms use exactly the same starting observation, saved noise, genuine positive/negative contexts and checkpoint. Commands differ only in the initial interaction pulse. One layout and one noise draw do not establish generalization.\n\nThe independent artifact audit passed: all 825 foundation values stayed unchanged, both complete latent trajectories and first-step guidance records verify, and all raw RGB-to-PNG mappings are exact. Source/input verification and sampled resource limits passed. The new A100 reports 2 MiB more reported total GPU memory than the training GPU; the reviewed compatibility check permits equal or greater capacity only, retaining exact other runtime fields and unchanged limits. The earlier rejected pre-execution check and revised source are retained.\n\nNine public transport parts and the derived index.json recover 443 files totaling 806,023,735 bytes. Transport totals 719,774,742 bytes. Only the original final part was split into two contiguous 44,887,371-byte pieces after upload connection failures. Their concatenation and the complete compressed stream match the original hashes exactly; all recovered file bytes and hashes are unchanged. The original eight-part recovery index remains available as original-index.json. The recovery contains all 100 saved latent states, all 34 native PNGs and raw RGB frames, both GIF previews, initial-step positive/negative/guided predictions, source copies, plans, metrics and logs. Later individual velocity arrays were not retained. Model weights and credentials are excluded.\n\nThe executed repository source is 099eeae6268da852b0acb580258e4c168f900520, retained in its source archive. The exact additional visual source and prepared input packet are in visual-transfer-v2.tar.gz. The publication tag points to the publication context. See LICENSE-NOTES.md and included component licenses for original code/data and attributed external Wan code.\n"
